{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f17e39d99b57bc5b12", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Atomic Physics - Test 2", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a684"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a63f", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5d8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2d"], "question": {"text": "Assuming the validity of Bohr's atomic model for hydrogen like ions the radius of $\\mathrm{Li}^{++}$ion in its ground state is given by $\\frac{1}{X} a_0$, where $X=$ _______. (Where $\\mathrm{a}_0$ is the first Bohr's radius.)"}, "options": [{"id": "96241f", "text": "2", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5d9"}, {"id": "2e6dde", "text": "1", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5da"}, {"id": "7e257b", "text": "3", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5db"}, {"id": "9c96ed", "text": "9", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5dc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5dd", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e43"], "question": {"text": "The ratio of the shortest wavelength of Balmer series to the shortest wavelength of Lyman series for hydrogen atom is :"}, "options": [{"id": "92d5b6", "text": "$4: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5de"}, {"id": "fccf57", "text": "$1: 4$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5df"}, {"id": "7900f8", "text": "$2: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5e0"}, {"id": "39d117", "text": "$1: 2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5e1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5e2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87d3"], "question": {"text": "Speed of an electron in Bohr&rsquo;s <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>7</mn><mi>th</mi></msup></math> orbit for Hydrogen atom is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The corresponding speed of the electron in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>rd</mi></msup></math> orbit, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is :"}, "options": [{"id": "5c07ca", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5e3"}, {"id": "a2c2c9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5e4"}, {"id": "3484da", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5e5"}, {"id": "e0afb2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5e6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5e7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5de3"], "question": {"text": "A particular hydrogen like ion emits radiation of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>92</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>15</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> when it makes transition from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. The frequency in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hz</mi></math> of radiation emitted in transition from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "3198f4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>57</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>15</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5e8"}, {"id": "a84f63", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>46</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>15</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5e9"}, {"id": "a0d8d8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>44</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>15</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5ea"}, {"id": "a02520", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>38</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>15</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5eb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5ec", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471c"], "question": {"text": "Radiation coming from transitions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> of hydrogen atoms fall on <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ions in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> states. The possible transition of helium ions as they absorb energy from the radiation is:"}, "options": [{"id": "03831c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5ed"}, {"id": "9ec2ac", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5ee"}, {"id": "8f19c6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5ef"}, {"id": "1e3285", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5f0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5f1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52c0"], "question": {"text": "A photon is emitted in transition from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> level in hydrogen atom. The corresponding wavelength for this transition is (given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "bddfe8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>941</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5f2"}, {"id": "09f2a4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>974</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5f3"}, {"id": "a02b7b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>99</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5f4"}, {"id": "c30301", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>94</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5f5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5f6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["6162fb5b6ed13040ec84df6b"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements</p><p><strong>Statement I:</strong> In hydrogen atom, the frequency of radiation emitted when an electron jumps from lower energy orbit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced></math>&nbsp;to higher energy orbit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced></math>, is given as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><strong>Statement II: </strong>The jumping of electron from higher energy orbit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced></math> to lower energy orbit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced></math> is associated with frequency of radiation given as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mstyle><mi>h</mi></mfrac></math>. This condition is Bohr&#39;s frequency condition.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7dfd63", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5f7"}, {"id": "999c2a", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5f8"}, {"id": "a6dd29", "text": "Statement I is correct but statement II is false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5f9"}, {"id": "fd275a", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but statement II is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5fa"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5fb", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e43"], "question": {"text": "The minimum energy required by a hydrogen atom in ground state to emit radiation in Balmer series is nearly :"}, "options": [{"id": "576663", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5fc"}, {"id": "811015", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5fd"}, {"id": "eecc8f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo> </mo><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5fe"}, {"id": "d238dc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5ff"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a600", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["6117b98967dbe2603c3ea31d"], "question": {"text": "The frequency of revolution of the electron in Bohr's orbit varies with $n$, the principal quantum number as"}, "options": [{"id": "556c47", "text": "$\\frac{1}{n^4}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a601"}, {"id": "a84b64", "text": "$\\frac{1}{n^2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a602"}, {"id": "aff8d8", "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a603"}, {"id": "343454", "text": "$\\frac{1}{n^3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a604"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a605", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5de3"], "question": {"text": "A free electron of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math> energy collides with a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;ion. This results in the formation of a hydrogen atom in the first excited state and a photon is released. Find the frequency of the emitted photon. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "7865b2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>27</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MHz</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a606"}, {"id": "49d781", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MHz</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a607"}, {"id": "ee17db", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>15</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MHz</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a608"}, {"id": "342ac5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>16</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MHz</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a609"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a60a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471c"], "question": {"text": "The energy required to ionise a hydrogen like ion in its ground state is <math><mn>9</mn></math> Rydbergs. What is the wavelength of the radiation emitted when the electron in this ion jumps from the second excited stale to the ground state?"}, "options": [{"id": "467469", "text": "<math><mn>24</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a60b"}, {"id": "f07ab1", "text": "<math><mn>11.4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a60c"}, {"id": "d330ed", "text": "<math><mn>35.8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a60d"}, {"id": "89393b", "text": "<math><mn>8.6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a60e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a60f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52c0"], "question": {"text": "<p>The energy levels of an hydrogen atom are shown below. The transition corresponding to emission of shortest wavelength is</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fc49ca28c-b0d7-476a-9cc1-c25d4