lns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a63b"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:01.999Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:01.999Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a682"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a680", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a664", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2d"], "question": {"text": "The radius of fifth orbit of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Li</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_______</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Take: radius of hydrogen atom<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>51</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></mover></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "f74740", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a665"}, {"id": "c5c248", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a666"}, {"id": "df5303", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a667"}, {"id": "0b6edb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a668"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a669", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52c0"], "question": {"text": "A hydrogen atom changes its state from $n=3$ to $n=2$. Due to recoil, the percentage change in the wave length of emitted light is approximately $1 \\times 10^{-n}$. The value of $n$ is_____. \n[Given $\\mathrm{Rhc}=13.6 \\mathrm{eV}, \\mathrm{hc}=1242 \\mathrm{eV} \\mathrm{nm}, \\mathrm{h}=6.6 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{~s}$ mass of the hydrogenatom $=1.6 \\times 10^{-27} \\mathrm{~kg}$ ]"}, "options": [{"id": "940a3b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a66a"}, {"id": "fedb8b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a66b"}, {"id": "00f0c2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a66c"}, {"id": "30cf53", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a66d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a66e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["6117b8be67dbe2603c3e8673"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e8594"], "question": {"text": "In Bohr&#39;s atomic model, the electron is assumed to revolve in a circular orbit of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8728;</mo></mover><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If the speed of electron is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then the current associated with the electron will be__________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi><mo>.</mo></math> [Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi></math> as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "2abe5b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a66f"}, {"id": "ae6f30", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a670"}, {"id": "28112b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a671"}, {"id": "793852", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a672"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a673", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3c"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5de3"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> is the ratio of energies of photons produced due to transition of an electron of hydrogen atom from its</p><p>(i) third permitted energy level to the second level and</p><p>(ii) the highest permitted energy level to the second permitted level.</p><p>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;will be</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "50a8cf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a674"}, {"id": "a154e9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a675"}, {"id": "1306b8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a676"}, {"id": "b161d7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a677"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a678", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ac"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4766"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471c"], "question": {"text": "An electron in the hydrogen atom initially in the fourth excited state makes a transition to $\\mathrm{n}^{\\text {th }}$ energy state by emitting a photon of energy 2.86 eV. The integer value of $n$ will be ____."}, "options": [{"id": "8efb49", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a679"}, {"id": "fef6cf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a67a"}, {"id": "2a2d02", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a67b"}, {"id": "5bc6a9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a67c"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:02.082Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:02.082Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f2e2ee0e063d924a683"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:16:01.658Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:58:01.408Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 25, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analysisVideoThumbnailDark": "", "shortTitle": "", "subjectDetails": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "title": "Physics", "shortName": "Phy"}], "testTimerType": "mm", "isMarkForReviewAvailable": true}, "temporaryTestDetail": {"_id": "6a4a1e7b9cbf3c6513046dd7", "testId": "69de21f17e39d99b57bc5b12", "userId": "6914cc9c4d7566258ee3a8fd", "startedAt": "2026-07-05T09:06:03.743Z", "lastAttemptedSection": null, "totalTimeLeft": 50, "bonusAttempt": false, "sections": [{"sectionId": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a63f", "questions": [{"questionId": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5d8", "markedOptions": [], "inputValue": null, "timeTaken": 0, "timeLeftWhenAttempted": null, "status": "notVisited", "_id": "6a4a1e7b9cbf3c6513046dd9", "uid": "6a4a1e7b9cbf3c6513046dda"}, {"questionId": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d924a5dd", "markedOptions": [], "inputVa